        {
          "id": "limiter_and_walls_numeric",
          "description": "Instantaneous numeric pin (time span 0 to 0, rel 1e-11) of the flux-law branches and wall regions the flux_law_numeric state leaves dormant. LIMITER: the thin cells (3,2) (h = 0.05 m, x neighbours 2.0/2.1 m) and (5,3) (h = 0.04 m, y neighbours 1.8/1.9 m) put the parabola's minimum below h_min_recon, so PPM_limit_pos scales both edges toward the mean with 0 < scale < 1 (scale ~ 0.09998 and ~ 0.09164); each is the upwind cell of one u/v < 0 and one u/v > 0 face. The vanished cells (4,5) (h = 5e-11 m, x) and (2,5) (h = 3e-11 m, y) have h <= h_min_recon = 1e-10 m inside a convex parabola, the scale = 0 (flat h_0) branch, so the flux is exactly dy*u*h. WALLS: the faces next to all four walls carry nonzero flux whose upwind stencils reach beyond the domain, pinning the clamped-index land closure against MOM6 with land cells outside the basin (uh(1,6), uh(1,1), uh(6,3), vh(6,1), vh(4,6)); the west/south divergence wall regions div_x(1,j) = IareaT*uh(1,j) and div_y(i,1) = IareaT*vh(i,1) are pinned at nonzero flux; and the east/north wall faces carry NONZERO velocity (u_E(7,3) = 0.03, v_N(4,7) = 0.025 m/s) so uh(7,3) = vh(4,7) = 0 tests the explicit wall regions rather than a zero velocity, with the telescoped wall divergences div_x(7,3) = -uh(6,3)*IareaT and div_y(4,7) = -vh(4,6)*IareaT. METRICS are non-uniform so a mis-bound metric shows: dxT by i = (8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 10, 9) m, dyT by j = (10, 9, 8, 10, 12, 11, 10) m, IdxT = 1/dxT(i), IdxT_e = 1/dxT(i+1) (the u < 0 upwind cell's), IdyT = 1/dyT(j), IdyT_n = 1/dyT(j+1), dy_Cu_E = dyT(j), dx_Cv_N = dxT(i), IareaT = 1/(dxT*dyT); dt = 150 s; mask all ocean. EXPECTED VALUES come from an independent numpy transcription of MOM_continuity_PPM.F90 (PPM_reconstruction_x/y F90:2397-2433, PPM_limit_pos F90:2665-2677, zonal_flux_layer F90:950-966 / merid_flux_layer F90:1852-1872) on the 7x7 basin padded with three land cells (mask2dT = 0, arbitrary thickness) on every side; the same transcription reproduces the 14 flux_law_numeric values exactly and is insensitive to the land-cell thickness.",
